{"id": "EUVD-2026-95023", "enisaUuid": "e221e184-de6f-31f3-a9e3-ebd1e58d9b7a", "description": "pH7Builder (pH7 Social Dating CMS) before 18.5.1 contains a payment validation vulnerability that allows registered low-privileged members to obtain any membership tier by supplying client-controlled plan and amount fields. Attackers can set item_number, cart_order_id, or the PayPal custom field while paying a token amount, or submit uncompleted PayPal IPN payments, to gain the most expensive membership and its paid features.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T14:10:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T17:52:19", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/commit/5218d017491fc855c0c788bd020e2376efdee76e", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/blob/v18.5.0/_protected/app/system/modules/payment/controllers/MainController.php#L274-L380", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ph7builder-before-18.5.1-payment-bypass-via-payment-module-maincontroller"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107636", "GHSA-32w5-672c-jvph"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c4fd4c48-d0f5-379b-8b82-a090ef199956", "product": {"name": "ph7builder", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}, "product_version": "0 <18.5.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "91208ae9-abe8-30e8-875e-733d50c3fdcb", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}], "isExploited": false}